## NO-GO

The cache is mostly safe, but I would not ship as-is because two edge cases violate the stated safety/revert requirements.

### Findings

**1. Boundary race can mark old-bucket data as new-bucket cache.**  
Refresh is decided before the fetch using current bucket, but the cache bucket is assigned after the fetch using a fresh `time.time()` call: [scanner.py](</Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main 1/src/market/scanner.py:780>) and [scanner.py](</Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main 1/src/market/scanner.py:853>). If a scan starts just before a 5m/15m boundary and finishes just after it, the fetched slug list may have been generated from the old bucket, while `_updown_*_cache_bucket` is set to the new bucket.

