**2. `scanner_slug_cache_enabled: false` is not byte-identical legacy behavior.**  
Disabled mode forces `refresh_* = True` via [scanner.py](</Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main 1/src/market/scanner.py:726>), so it does fetch every cycle. However, the refresh branch still writes caches and still falls back to cached markets on failed/timeout fetches: [scanner.py](</Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main 1/src/market/scanner.py:843>) and [scanner.py](</Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main 1/src/market/scanner.py:885>). Old behavior would return the live fetch result, usually `[]` on failure. So the flag does not fully bypass the cache.

